identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/layoutDirectionBehavior(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"layoutDirectionBehavior","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI23LayoutDirectionBehaviorO","text":"LayoutDirectionBehavior","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/layoutdirectionbehavior(_:)","abstract":[],"title":"layoutDirectionBehavior(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/layoutDirectionBehavior(_:)","role":"symbol"}}}